verification_core/ft4d is an original implementation written for this project,
based on the dataset fault tree analysis (FT4D) method described in:

  Toshiaki Aoki, Daisuke Kawakami, Nobuo Chida, Takashi Tomita.
  "Dataset Fault Tree Analysis for Systematic Evaluation of Machine Learning
  Systems." In 2020 IEEE 25th Pacific Rim International Symposium on Dependable
  Computing (PRDC), pp. 100-109, 2020. doi:10.1109/PRDC50213.2020.00021

Third-party software
--------------------
The following projects are NOT included in this repository. They are required
for the AWSIM target and must be obtained separately from their authors under
their own terms:

- AWSIM-Labs (simulator):       https://github.com/duongtd23/AWSIM-Labs
- AW-Runtime-Monitor
  (incl. aw_monitor msg/srv):   https://github.com/duongtd23/AW-Runtime-Monitor
- AW-CheckerPy
  (aw_checkerpy.py, *.maude):   https://github.com/duongtd23/AW-CheckerPy
  D. D. Tran, T. Tomita, T. Aoki. "Safety Analysis of Autonomous Driving Systems:
  A Simulation-Based Runtime Verification Approach." IEEE Transactions on
  Reliability, 74(4):4574-4588, 2025. doi:10.1109/TR.2025.3561455
- Autoware:                     https://github.com/autowarefoundation/autoware
- PRISM:                        https://github.com/prismmodelchecker/prism
- Maude:                        https://github.com/maude-lang/Maude

AW_Kinematics_Extractor/ re-implements, in Python, the kinematics and TTC logic
specified in the AW-CheckerPy Maude specifications.
